# L1: no derivative at a delta = 1 coordinate with at most one incident departure

Alexander Richard Towell, with Claude Code (Anthropic) assistance. Proposed
written lemmas plus an exact cover and certificates (`cases018.py`,
`cover_reader018.py`, `model018.py`, `certify018.py`, `reader018.py`).
Reviewed by Codex (REVIEW-L1-codex.md): sound after the fixes applied
here. Not frozen. Global status: OPEN.

## Setting

The empty-pair selfdual representative (1513 lines 7-9): f(0) = 0, f = 1
on every input of weight 1 or 2, h = 1 - 2f, k_S = 16 h_hat(S) at levels
1, 3, 5. Baseline: singleton k in {1,2}, cubic k in {-1,0}, quintic k in
{0,1}; negative quintics have magnitude m; every other departure costs at
least 2 (singleton 0 or 3, cubic -2 or +1, quintic 2) and the total
departure cost is the residual r.

Let u lie in exactly one negative quintic Q + u (delta(u) = 1). Then
p = Delta_u f on the other 13 coordinates satisfies 16p = k_u + sum_ab
k_uab chi_ab + sum_abcd k_uabcd chi_abcd, p in {-1,0,1}, p(0) = 1,
p(e_v) = f(e_u + e_v) - 1 = 0, ordinary quadratic coefficients
f(1_uab) in {0,1}; the quartic Q has numerator -m, and only departures
whose support contains u appear in p.

## Claim

For m in {1,2}: no such p exists when at most one residual departure
contains u and that departure (if any) has cost 2. (Every residual
departure costs 2 or at least 6; in (2^4) and (2^4,1) the residual is 4 or
2, so cost-6 departures cannot occur there.)

## Why this closes (2^4) and (2^4,1) (counting)

(2^4) has r = 4 (at most two cost-2 departures) and m = 2 on every
support; sum over coordinates of (delta - 1) is 5N - 14 = 6, so at least 8
coordinates have delta = 1. Two distinct departure supports share at most
4 coordinates, so at least 4 of them meet at most one departure. (2^4,1)
has r = 2 (at most one departure), m in {1,2}, and at least
14 - (25 - 14) = 3 coordinates with delta = 1. In both, union 14 is forced
(no-free-frontier.json). So L1 excludes both inventories outright.

## Lemmas used by the cover

1. Triangle incidence (for the types other than a +2 quartic, which item 4
   excludes first). For a triple T not inside Q every quartic containing
   T is unit, and T contains a pair outside Q that is not the departure
   pair (T has at least two pairs not inside Q). That pair's link is empty,
   C4 or C5, so the incidence of T is 0 or 2: t_T is binary. Inside Q,
   t_T = (-m + s)/2 with s the number of unit quartics T + y (y outside Q,
   so s <= 9), hence t_T is an integer in [-1, 6] (m = 1 forces s odd,
   m = 2 even); `model018.py` encodes it exactly as t + 2 t2 + 4 t4 - 1.
2. Ordinary vertices (outside Q and the departure support). Every pair
   through such a vertex v has a unit link (no quartic through v is Q),
   empty, C4 or C5, and P_v = 2 D_v - 4 holds with the weights, so the unit
   link of v is a union of closed surfaces with chi = 2 and degrees 4, 5:
   a sphere, hence one of the six deltahedra (017 NEAR-FLAG.md table, from
   the 015 enumeration), or two six-vertex projective planes (each
   component has chi >= 1; a chi = 1 component with degrees <= 5 has six
   vertices, all of degree 5). The identities give E = 49 + c also here.
3. Flag rows at ordinary vertices with a sphere link: the deltahedra are
   flag (017 `near_flag.py`).
4. +2 quartic departure D. D != Q, so D has a vertex x outside Q; x lies in
   no other departure, every pair through x is baseline, and the only
   non-unit quartic through x is D. The accepted private-vertex argument
   (`006/two-exception-positive-extension.md`, accepted in
   `006/independent-math-audit/connected-six-unit-exclusion-audit.md`,
   re-reviewed in 016) uses only these data at x and gives a unit link
   with Euler characteristic 3, impossible. So these types need no cover.
5. Pair departure with an endpoint x outside Q. Every pair through x except
   the departure pair has a unit link C4 or C5 (or empty); the departure
   pair's link is C6 or two triangles (-2) or C3 (+1); no non-unit quartic
   contains x. This is the setting of 017 VERTEX-TYPES.md Lemma 2 at x, so
   its link is one of the three type (1,0) spheres (orders 9, 10, 11; a
   lone split partner is impossible) or the type (0,1) sphere (order 7),
   with the partner y at its degree-6 or degree-3 vertex. A bowtie link of
   xy centred at z would put xyz in four tetrahedra, but xz is baseline,
   avoids Q and has a cycle link, so incidence at most 2. A lone split
   partner gives chi = 3 on at most 13 vertices; both degree-3 copies lie
   in a sphere component, which needs at least 8 vertices for their
   disjoint neighbourhoods, and the six-vertex projective plane makes 14.

## Cover

Fix a derivative of an allowed type. Either some ordinary vertex has a
disconnected link (part A: root there, link two six-vertex projective
planes on all twelve other coordinates; no flag rows), or every ordinary
link is a deltahedron. In the latter case root at an ordinary vertex
of maximum degree among the ordinary vertices (part B-ord) for the types
without a pair or with the pair inside Q (so every other ordinary vertex
has degree at most the root link's order: the `degcap` rows), or at
the pair's endpoint outside Q (part B-exc); flag rows at all other ordinary
vertices. Placements of Q and the pair are taken up to root-link
automorphisms and non-neighbour relabelling (`cases018.py`; 2221 cases;
`cover_reader018.py` checks every labelled placement).

## Status

Certificates running (`run018.py`, 4442 = 2221 x 2 magnitude obligations;
a certificate may cover several (type, m) variants when every stored row
coincides, checked by the reader). The reader proves only that the stored
case's rows are infeasible; `read_all018.py` binds each certificate to its
cover case by comparing every case field (including root metadata), and
requires every (case, m) obligation. The cover keeps 154 redundant cases
(non-neighbour relabelling inside Q is not quotiented); this costs time
only.
"""Exact row model of one derivative with a negative quartic (lemma L1).

p = Delta_u f on N = 13 coordinates, 16p = c + sum_A k_A chi_A + sum_D l_D chi_D.
Baseline: k_A = -kappa_A in {-1,0}, l_D in {0,1}. Fixed exceptions: pair
numerators given in `exceptions`; quartics with fixed weight w (l_D = w, a
variable fixed to 1 carrying coefficient w); the constant c in [c_lo, c_hi].
Ordinary expansion (as in 017 model.py): m_A = (k_A + L_A)/4 in {0,1},
cubic -t_T with t_T = L_T / 2, quartic l_D, hence the rows

  pair      4 m_A - L_A - k_A = 0
  triple    L_T - 2 t_T = 0
  vertex    K_v + P_v = 8                    (p(e_v) = 0)
  constant  16 - c_hi <= K + L <= 16 - c_lo  (p(0) = 1)
  value     0 <= |X| - sum m + sum t - sum l <= 2, every X with |X| >= 2

where L_S = sum over D containing S of l_D (weights included). t_T is
binary (incidence 0 or 2) except on `int_triples`, where
t_T = b0 + 2 b1 + 4 b2 - 1 in [-1, 6] (names t, t2, t4). Flag rows at
`flag_vertices`: t_vab + t_vbd + t_vad - l_vabd <= 2. Implied rows: the
linear consequences P_v = 2 D_v - 4 and K_v = 12 - 2 D_v.
Rows are (terms, lo, hi, key) over variable indices, as in 014 and 017.
"""
import itertools
import sys

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
N = 13


def build(exceptions, c_lo, c_hi, weights=(), int_triples=(), flag_vertices=(), implied=True, n=N, degree_cap=None):
    V = range(n)
    pairs = [frozenset(p) for p in itertools.combinations(V, 2)]
    triples = [frozenset(t) for t in itertools.combinations(V, 3)]
    quads = [frozenset(q) for q in itertools.combinations(V, 4)]
    weights = {frozenset(q): w for q, w in dict(weights).items()}
    ints = {frozenset(t) for t in int_triples}
    exc = {frozenset(p): k for p, k in dict(exceptions).items()}
    names = ([('l', q) for q in quads] + [('m', a) for a in pairs] + [('t', t) for t in triples]
             + [('kappa', a) for a in pairs if a not in exc]
             + [(nm, t) for t in sorted(ints, key=sorted) for nm in ('t2', 't4')])
    index = {v: i for i, v in enumerate(names)}
    rows = []

    def emit(acc, const, lo, hi, key):
        terms = sorted((index[nm], co) for nm, co in acc.items() if co)
        rows.append((terms, lo - const, hi - const, key))

    def add(acc, nm, co):
        acc[nm] = acc.get(nm, 0) + co

    def add_l(acc, q, co):
        add(acc, ('l', q), co * weights.get(q, 1))

    def add_k(acc, a, co):
        """Add co * k_a; return the constant part."""
        if a in exc:
            return co * exc[a]
        add(acc, ('kappa', a), -co)
        return 0

    def add_t(acc, T, co):
        """Add co * t_T; return the constant part."""
        add(acc, ('t', T), co)
        if T in ints:
            add(acc, ('t2', T), 2 * co)
            add(acc, ('t4', T), 4 * co)
            return -co
        return 0

    for a in pairs:
        acc = {('m', a): 4}
        for q in quads:
            if a <= q:
                add_l(acc, q, -1)
        const = add_k(acc, a, -1)
        emit(acc, const, 0, 0, ('pair', tuple(sorted(a))))
    for T in triples:
        acc = {}
        for q in quads:
            if T <= q:
                add_l(acc, q, 1)
        const = add_t(acc, T, -2)
        emit(acc, const, 0, 0, ('triple', tuple(sorted(T))))
    for v in V:
        acc, const = {}, 0
        for a in pairs:
            if v in a:
                const += add_k(acc, a, 1)
        for q in quads:
            if v in q:
                add_l(acc, q, 1)
        emit(acc, const, 8, 8, ('vertex', v))
    acc, const = {}, 0
    for a in pairs:
        const += add_k(acc, a, 1)
    for q in quads:
        add_l(acc, q, 1)
    emit(acc, const, 16 - c_hi, 16 - c_lo, ('constant',))
    for size in range(2, n + 1):
        for X in itertools.combinations(V, size):
            xs = frozenset(X)
            acc, const = {}, 0
            for a in pairs:
                if a <= xs:
                    add(acc, ('m', a), -1)
            for T in triples:
                if T <= xs:
                    const += add_t(acc, T, 1)
            for q in quads:
                if q <= xs:
                    add_l(acc, q, -1)
            emit(acc, const, -size, 2 - size, ('value', X))
    for v in sorted(flag_vertices):
        for a, b, d in itertools.combinations([x for x in V if x != v], 3):
            acc, const = {}, 0
            for x, y in ((a, b), (b, d), (a, d)):
                const += add_t(acc, frozenset((v, x, y)), 1)
            add_l(acc, frozenset((v, a, b, d)), -1)
            emit(acc, const, -10 ** 6, 2, ('flag', v, (a, b, d)))
    if degree_cap is not None:                     # (bound, vertices): D_v <= bound
        bound, cap_vertices = degree_cap
        for v in sorted(cap_vertices):
            acc = {('m', a): 1 for a in pairs if v in a}
            emit(acc, 0, -10 ** 6, bound, ('degcap', v))
    if implied:
        for v in V:
            acc = {}
            for q in quads:
                if v in q:
                    add_l(acc, q, 1)
            for a in pairs:
                if v in a:
                    add(acc, ('m', a), -2)
            emit(acc, 0, -4, -4, ('implied_P', v))
            acc, const = {}, 0
            for a in pairs:
                if v in a:
                    const += add_k(acc, a, 1)
                    add(acc, ('m', a), 2)
            emit(acc, const, 12, 12, ('implied_k', v))
    return dict(variables=names, rows=rows)


def root_fixings(root, link_faces, n=N):
    nbrs = set().union(*[set(f) for f in link_faces])
    out = {('m', frozenset((root, v))): int(v in nbrs) for v in range(n) if v != root}
    faces = {frozenset(f) for f in link_faces}
    for f in itertools.combinations([v for v in range(n) if v != root], 3):
        out[('l', frozenset(f) | {root})] = int(frozenset(f) in faces)
    return out


def case_model(case, m):
    """Model and fixings for one cover case at negative magnitude m."""
    Q = frozenset(case['Q'])
    t = case['type']
    exc = {}
    if t in ('pm', 'pp'):
        exc[frozenset(case['pair'])] = -2 if t == 'pm' else 1
    c_lo, c_hi = {'none': (1, 2), 'c0': (0, 0), 'c3': (3, 3)}.get(t, (1, 2))
    special = set(Q) | set(case['pair'])
    flags = [] if case['part'] == 'A' else [v for v in range(1, N) if v not in special]
    # in part B-ord the root is an ordinary vertex of maximum degree (L1.md), so every
    # other ordinary vertex has degree at most the root link's order
    cap = (case['order'], flags) if case['part'] == 'B-ord' else None
    model = build(exc, c_lo, c_hi, weights={Q: -m}, flag_vertices=flags, degree_cap=cap,
                  int_triples=[frozenset(T) for T in itertools.combinations(sorted(Q), 3)])
    fixed = root_fixings(0, case['faces'])
    fixed[('l', Q)] = 1
    return model, fixed
"""Certify one L1 cover case (018): core rows -> CNF -> CaDiCaL LRAT -> pinned lrat-trim.

Adapted from 017 certify017.py (frozen); only the model builder differs.

Untrusted producer. The case's rows (model.py) have the root fixings
substituted (fixed variables removed, bounds shifted), which is sound: if the
substituted rows have no 0/1 solution on the free variables, the case has
none. A CP-SAT assumption core and a deletion pass pick a row subset; the
014 decision-diagram encoder writes its CNF; CaDiCaL proves UNSAT with LRAT;
lrat-trim checks it. The certificate stores the variable names, the chosen
rows (key, ordered terms by name, bounds) and the file hashes, so that
reader017.py can rebuild every row independently.

  certify017.py CASE_JSON --c C --stem STEM [--core-seconds S] [--test-seconds T]
"""
import argparse
import hashlib
import json
import subprocess
import sys
import time
from pathlib import Path

sys.dont_write_bytecode = True
HERE = Path(__file__).resolve().parent
sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE))
sys.path.insert(0, str(HERE.parent / '014-context-pricing'))
import model018 as mdl  # noqa: E402
from encode import CNF  # noqa: E402

ROOT = HERE.parents[2]
CADICAL = ROOT / 'build/solvers/cadical-3.0.1/build/cadical'
LRAT_TRIM = HERE.parent / '006-solver-resume/lrat-trim/lrat-trim'
LRAT_TRIM_SHA = '179d041f645a98d51d3ca6dbbe4950806ad8eceb54c9a762f54e7acee154f8df'


def sha(path):
    return hashlib.sha256(Path(path).read_bytes()).hexdigest()


def substituted(case, m):
    model, fixed = mdl.case_model(case, m)
    names = model['variables']
    value = {i: fixed[nm] for i, nm in enumerate(names) if nm in fixed}
    rows = []
    for terms, lo, hi, key in model['rows']:
        shift = sum(co * value[v] for v, co in terms if v in value)
        rest = [(v, co) for v, co in terms if v not in value]
        if not rest:
            if not lo <= shift <= hi:
                raise SystemExit(f'fixings violate row {key}')
            continue
        rows.append((rest, lo - shift, hi - shift, key))
    return dict(variables=names, rows=rows)


def check(m, subset, seconds, assume=False, workers=1):
    from ortools.sat.python import cp_model
    cp = cp_model.CpModel()
    x = [cp.NewBoolVar(f'x{i}') for i in range(len(m['variables']))]
    lits = {}
    for k in subset:
        terms, lo, hi, _ = m['rows'][k]
        con = cp.AddLinearConstraint(sum(co * x[v] for v, co in terms), lo, hi)
        if assume:
            a = cp.NewBoolVar(f'a{k}')
            con.OnlyEnforceIf(a)
            lits[k] = a
    if assume:
        cp.AddAssumptions(list(lits.values()))
    s = cp_model.CpSolver()
    s.parameters.max_time_in_seconds = seconds
    s.parameters.num_workers = 1 if assume else workers
    st = s.StatusName(s.Solve(cp))
    core = None
    if assume and st == 'INFEASIBLE':
        idx = {a.Index(): k for k, a in lits.items()}
        core = sorted(idx[i] for i in s.SufficientAssumptionsForInfeasibility())
    return st, core


def run(argv, log, timeout):
    t = time.time()
    p = subprocess.run(argv, capture_output=True, text=True, timeout=timeout)
    Path(log).write_text(p.stdout + '\n--- stderr ---\n' + p.stderr)
    return p.returncode, p.stdout, round(time.time() - t, 2)


def jname(nm):
    return [nm[0], sorted(nm[1])]


def jkey(key):
    return [key[0]] + [list(x) if isinstance(x, tuple) else x for x in key[1:]]


LARGE = 30


def certify(case, mag, stem, core_seconds, test_seconds, timeout=3600, delete_budget=600, seed_k=None):
    t0 = time.time()
    m = substituted(case, mag)
    if seed_k is not None:
        # structural subset, no CP-SAT: every non-value row and the value rows with |X| <= seed_k
        keep = [i for i, r in enumerate(m['rows']) if r[3][0] != 'value' or len(r[3][1]) <= seed_k]
        core = keep
        delete_budget = 0
    else:
        st, core = check(m, range(len(m['rows'])), core_seconds, assume=True)
        if core is None:
            return dict(status='NO_CORE', solver=st)
        keep = list(core)
    # deletion pass over the rows that are expensive to encode, largest first, within a time budget
    t_del = time.time()
    for k in sorted(core, key=lambda k: -len(m['rows'][k][0])):
        if len(m['rows'][k][0]) <= LARGE or time.time() - t_del > delete_budget:
            break
        trial = [j for j in keep if j != k]
        if check(m, trial, test_seconds)[0] == 'INFEASIBLE':
            keep = trial
    cnf = CNF(len(m['variables']))
    for k in keep:
        terms, lo, hi, _ = m['rows'][k]
        cnf.add_row([(v + 1, co) for v, co in terms], lo, hi, tag=k)
    cnf_path, proof, labels_path = Path(stem + '.cnf'), Path(stem + '.lrat'), Path(stem + '.labels.json')
    cnf_path.write_text(cnf.dimacs())
    labels_path.write_text(json.dumps([[v, *cnf.labels[v]] for v in sorted(cnf.labels)]))
    if sha(LRAT_TRIM) != LRAT_TRIM_SHA:
        raise SystemExit('lrat-trim binary changed')
    rc, _, t_solve = run([str(CADICAL), '--lrat=true', '--binary=false', '-q', str(cnf_path), str(proof)],
                         stem + '.cadical.log', timeout)
    # variants (type, magnitude) whose substituted rows coincide with these, row by row
    keys = {m['rows'][k][3]: (m['rows'][k][0], m['rows'][k][1], m['rows'][k][2]) for k in keep}
    variants = []
    types = ['none', 'c0', 'c3'] if case['type'] in ('none', 'c0', 'c3') else [case['type']]
    for t2 in types:
        for m2 in (1, 2):
            if (t2, m2) == (case['type'], mag):
                variants.append([t2, m2])
                continue
            alt = substituted(dict(case, type=t2), m2)
            alt_rows = {r[3]: (r[0], r[1], r[2]) for r in alt['rows']}
            if alt['variables'] == m['variables'] and all(alt_rows.get(key) == val for key, val in keys.items()):
                variants.append([t2, m2])
    rec = dict(case=case, magnitude=mag, variants=variants, seed_k=seed_k, variables=[jname(nm) for nm in m['variables']],
               rows=[dict(id=k, key=jkey(m['rows'][k][3]),
                          terms=[[jname(m['variables'][v]), co] for v, co in m['rows'][k][0]],
                          lo=m['rows'][k][1], hi=m['rows'][k][2]) for k in keep],
               core_initial=len(core),
               cnf=dict(path=str(cnf_path), sha256=sha(cnf_path), variables=cnf.nvars, clauses=len(cnf.clauses)),
               labels=dict(path=str(labels_path), sha256=sha(labels_path)),
               solver='UNSAT' if rc == 20 else f'rc{rc}', solve_wall=t_solve)
    if rc == 20:
        rc2, out2, t_chk = run([str(LRAT_TRIM), '--forward', '--no-trim', str(cnf_path), str(proof)],
                               stem + '.lrat-trim.log', timeout)
        ok = rc2 == 20 and any(line.strip() == 's VERIFIED' for line in out2.splitlines())
        rec.update(proof=dict(path=str(proof), sha256=sha(proof), bytes=proof.stat().st_size),
                   lrat_trim=dict(sha256=LRAT_TRIM_SHA, exit=rc2, wall=t_chk),
                   status='LRAT_VERIFIED_CORE_UNSAT' if ok else 'LRAT_NOT_VERIFIED')
    else:
        rec['status'] = 'NO_PROOF'
    rec['wall'] = round(time.time() - t0, 1)
    Path(stem + '.json').write_text(json.dumps(rec) + '\n')
    return dict(status=rec['status'], rows=len(keep), clauses=len(cnf.clauses), wall=rec['wall'], variants=variants)


def main():
    ap = argparse.ArgumentParser()
    ap.add_argument('case'); ap.add_argument('--m', type=int, required=True); ap.add_argument('--stem', required=True)
    ap.add_argument('--core-seconds', type=float, default=600); ap.add_argument('--test-seconds', type=float, default=10)
    a = ap.parse_args()
    case = json.loads(Path(a.case).read_text())
    print(json.dumps(certify(case, a.m, a.stem, a.core_seconds, a.test_seconds)))


if __name__ == '__main__':
    main()

